{"t": 1794117808.0281808, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return one page of ``items``.\n\n    ``number`` is 1-based, matching the API's ``?page=`` parameter, so\n    ``number=1`` returns the first page.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "fix(pager): treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794117814.8419595, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\n\n`page()` treated the page number as 0-based: `start = number * size`, so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page while the API documents `?page=1` as the first page.\n\nThe offset is now computed as `(number - 1) * size`, making `page(items, 1, size)` return the first page and keeping subsequent pages aligned with the documented 1-based numbering.\n\nFixes #57.\n\n## Testing\n\n```python\n>>> from catalog.pager import page\n>>> page(list(range(10)), 1, 3)\n[0, 1, 2]\n>>> page(list(range(10)), 2, 3)\n[3, 4, 5]\n>>> page(list(range(10)), 4, 3)\n[9]\n```", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "fix(pager): make page numbers 1-based (#57)"}, "ok": true}
